---
// The QA skill's showcase. Hand-authored, and sharing the `.topology` classes
// with every other skill diagram on purpose, so they read as one visual
// language and all track the site theme.
// Source facts: src/content/cards/qa.md, docs/context/testing.md.
//
// Marker and aria ids are namespaced (`qa-`) because several diagrams render on
// the same page and duplicate ids would silently point at the wrong element.
---

<figure class="card-diagram">
  <div class="card-diagram-scroll">
    <svg
      class="topology"
      viewBox="0 0 820 300"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="qa-loop-title qa-loop-desc"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      fill="none"
    >
      <title id="qa-loop-title">The QA-to-implementer loop</title>
      <desc id="qa-loop-desc">
        A four-step cycle. One: the requirement, a definition of done written
        before any work starts. Two: the agent implements, in the implementer's
        seat and never the reviewer's. Three: CI gates act as automated
        acceptance criteria and are cleared first. Four: I verify the work
        against the requirement. Failing work is rejected with specifics and
        returns to step two, looping until nothing is outstanding. Only once the
        goal is confirmed reached does step five run, updating the
        documentation.
      </desc>

      <defs>
        <marker id="qa-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path class="arrow-head" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" stroke="none" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- rejection loop, drawn above the row so it never crosses the flow -->
      <path class="link ephemeral-link" d="M716,76 L716,46 L308,46 L308,76" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />
      <text class="wire" x="512" y="38" text-anchor="middle">rejected — with specifics, and it loops until nothing is outstanding</text>

      <!-- 1. Requirement -->
      <rect class="node" x="15" y="76" width="178" height="80" rx="10" />
      <text class="label" x="29" y="100">1 · Requirement</text>
      <text class="sub" x="29" y="118">Definition of done, written</text>
      <text class="sub" x="29" y="134">before any work starts</text>

      <path class="link" d="M195,116 L217,116" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />

      <!-- 2. Agent implements -->
      <rect class="node" x="219" y="76" width="178" height="80" rx="10" />
      <text class="label" x="233" y="100">2 · Agent implements</text>
      <text class="sub" x="233" y="118">in the implementer's seat</text>
      <text class="sub" x="233" y="134">— never the reviewer's</text>

      <path class="link" d="M399,116 L421,116" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />

      <!-- 3. CI gates -->
      <rect class="node" x="423" y="76" width="178" height="80" rx="10" />
      <text class="label" x="437" y="100">3 · CI gates</text>
      <text class="sub" x="437" y="118">automated acceptance</text>
      <text class="sub" x="437" y="134">criteria, cleared first</text>

      <path class="link" d="M603,116 L625,116" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />

      <!-- 4. I verify -->
      <rect class="node" x="627" y="76" width="178" height="80" rx="10" />
      <text class="label" x="641" y="100">4 · I verify</text>
      <text class="sub" x="641" y="118">against the requirement,</text>
      <text class="sub" x="641" y="134">not against how it feels</text>

      <!-- accept path -->
      <path class="link" d="M716,156 L716,206" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />
      <text class="wire accent" x="726" y="186">accepted</text>

      <!-- 5. Docs -->
      <rect class="node" x="627" y="206" width="178" height="70" rx="10" />
      <text class="label" x="641" y="230">5 · Docs updated</text>
      <text class="sub" x="641" y="248">only once the goal is</text>
      <text class="sub" x="641" y="264">confirmed reached</text>

      <text class="wire accent" x="15" y="234">0 self-certified merges</text>
      <text class="wire" x="15" y="254">the implementer never judges their own work — and that</text>
      <text class="wire" x="15" y="270">stays true when the implementer is a language model</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    The loop runs the same whether the implementer is a person or a model. Step 3 is the
    part that scales: CI gates are the acceptance criteria a human would otherwise check
    by hand, so step 4 only ever looks at work that already passes.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
